# f1 = match, f3 = join
# `match` calls itself by the value of its own variable and hands what came back, behind a test for null, to `join`, which goes by what its callers leave. In the slow body the record of that call says anything (a slow body reads no tables);
# the walk knows by what `match` hands back that it is a list and lays no check. The judge of calls follows the same way: through the Narrowed, where what the test took away is apart from what it left.
# RUN(SLOW): walk f1:SlowBody mechanisms=all
# SLOW: = Call {{*}}calleeName="match"
# SLOW: = Narrowed
# SLOW: = CallDirect {{*}}function=f3
# RUN(UNCHECKED): walk f1:SlowBody mechanisms=all
# UNCHECKED: code f1:SlowBody
# UNCHECKED-NOT: CheckProof {{*}}checkedType=null|Array
# RUN(SILENT): walk f1:SlowBody mechanisms=all
# SILENT: code f1:SlowBody
# SILENT-NOT: TypeOutOfDate
